module std where

-- =========================================================================
-- Nat ⇄ Number / Nat ⇄ NonNegInt bridges (numeric-tower Phase 1).
--
-- The opaque-boundary crossings the D7 law and the D8 iso need. `Nat` is
-- `$opaque { repr:"number", pure: Zero | Succ pred:Nat }`: in production the
-- runtime stores a JS number (the repr); the pure Peano value is the
-- semantics. These two bridges materialize / count the Peano structure so the
-- pure bodies (nat-arith.fenel) can be exercised against the opaque `number`
-- rep on small samples. representation-substrate Phase 2 flipped these to the
-- POSITIONAL `Succ x` / `Succ p` surface (canonical `{$tag:"Succ", _0:…}`),
-- retiring the numeric-tower Phase-1 named-field workaround: the construct gap
-- is dissolved (Nat is now a registered entity ⇒ the registry `$opaque`-peel
-- indexes `Zero`/`Succ` — see nat-arith.fenel header). numberToNat/natToNumber
-- ARE the `Reprable JsRuntime Nat` lower/lift (fenel/std/dispatch-instances.fenel).
--
--   numberToNat : Number -> Nat   builds Succ^n Zero by counting down from n.
--   natToNumber : Nat -> Number   counts the Succ wrappers.
--
-- numberToNat is the production native's INVERSE direction only for the law/
-- iso oracle — production arithmetic stays on the native `number` fast path;
-- these never run on the hot path.

@label "Number to Nat"
@description "Materialize a non-negative whole Number as a Peano Nat (Succ^n Zero). numberToNat n = if n <= 0 then Zero else Succ (numberToNat (n - 1)). For n <= 0 (and the fractional part of any non-integer) it returns the floor-clamped-to-Zero Peano value — the bridge is defined over the Nat domain [0,∞). Terminates by the guarded Number decrement (below the totality checker's Nat rungs ⇒ Unknown; total over the intended ℕ domain)."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano" "bridge"
numberToNat : (n: Number) -> Nat
numberToNat n = if lte n 0 then Zero else Succ (numberToNat (sub n 1))

@label "Nat to Number"
@description "Explicit approximate projection to finite Number. Its input refinement admits only values with a finite current projection; approximateNat returns a typed refusal otherwise. Exact arithmetic and text do not use this projection."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano" "bridge"
natToNumber : (n: FiniteNumberProjectableNat) -> Number
natToNumber n = integerNumberProjectionRaw n

-- D8 — the inductive↔refinement iso witnesses (Nat ≅ { n:Int | n >= 0 }).
-- numeric-tower audit §3 D8: each rung has an inductive presentation (Peano)
-- AND a refinement presentation (NonNegInt = $refined Int [0,∞),
-- type-foundation.ts:1481), connected by an iso = a witness PAIR + the
-- round-trip laws (proof = inhabitant — [[feedback_laws_supers_are_el_dependent_typing]]),
-- NOT a `Presentations` class (the typeclasses-are-types trap, D8a-rejected).
-- For Nat the witnesses are exactly the bridges re-typed to the refinement
-- codomain/domain (NonNegInt repr is `number`), so they are cheap to
-- CONSTRUCT here (not merely state). The round-trip laws —
--   natFromRefined (natToRefined n) ≡ n   (Nat side)
--   natToRefined (natFromRefined m) ≡ m   (NonNegInt side)
-- are stated here and sample-discharged in nat-peano.test.ts; their `$el`
-- law-field home on the rung type lands with the Phase-5 class minting (the
-- same deferral as the D7 law — there is no class/type slot to hang `$el`
-- law fields on at Phase 1).

@label "Nat to NonNegInt"
@description "Embed an exact Nat as the nonnegative Int refinement through all its integer digits. No Number projection occurs."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano" "iso"
natToRefined : (n: Nat) -> NonNegInt
natToRefined n = integerIntEncodeDigits (natToExactText n)

@label "NonNegInt to Nat"
@description "Restore the exact nonnegative Int refinement as Nat through its integer digits. No Number projection occurs."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano" "iso"
natFromRefined : (n: NonNegInt) -> Nat
natFromRefined n = integerNatEncodeDigits (intToExactText n)
